<Project>
  <ItemGroup Condition="$(NBGV_PublicRelease) != 'True' AND '$(CODEQL_RUNNER)' == '' AND '$(Dockerbuild)' != 'true'">
    <!-- Note: Versions such as 3.6.146, where known working for 4 digit versioning -->
    <PackageReference Include="Nerdbank.GitVersioning">
      <PrivateAssets>all</PrivateAssets>
      <IncludeAssets>runtime; build; native; contentfiles; analyzers; buildtransitive</IncludeAssets>
    </PackageReference>
  </ItemGroup>
  <!-- set version manually in docker builds -->
  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(Dockerbuild)' == 'true'">
    <GenerateAssemblyInfo>true</GenerateAssemblyInfo>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <!-- NBGV_ variables are only available in cloud build -->
  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(NBGV_PublicRelease)' == 'True'">
    <Version>$(NBGV_Version)$(NBGV_PrereleaseVersion)</Version>
    <VersionPrefix>$(NBGV_SimpleVersion)</VersionPrefix>
    <VersionSuffix>$(NBGV_VersionRevision)$(NBGV_PrereleaseVersion)</VersionSuffix>
    <AssemblyVersion>$(NBGV_SimpleVersion)</AssemblyVersion>
    <FileVersion>$(NBGV_Version)</FileVersion>
    <PackageVersion>$(NBGV_Version)$(NBGV_PrereleaseVersion)</PackageVersion>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <!--
    Do not let Nerdbank.GitVersioning publish cloud build variables from inside
    MSBuild. Its SetCloudBuildVersionVars target runs once per project, and on
    GitHub Actions the provider implements "set a variable" as an append to the
    file named by $GITHUB_ENV. Builds here are deliberately parallel across
    MSBuild nodes (see the Build step in .github/workflows/buildandtest.yml), so
    several nodes append GitAssemblyInformationalVersion / GitBuildVersion /
    GitBuildVersionSimple to that one file concurrently. Interleaved appends tear
    a line, and the runner then rejects the leftover fragment after the compile
    has already succeeded:

        Build succeeded.  0 Error(s)
        ##[error]Unable to process file command 'env' successfully.
        ##[error]Invalid format '7'

    ('7' being the tail of a torn `GitBuildVersion=2.0.3x7.yyyyy`.) See issue
    #4458.

    Nothing reads these three variables: every workflow and pipeline that
    consumes version information runs .azurepipelines/set-version.ps1 first, and
    `nbgv cloud -c -a` there writes the same Git* variables plus the NBGV_* set
    that version.props and common.props actually use - once, from a single
    process, with no concurrency. This leaves that script as the only writer.

    Note this is deliberately an MSBuild property rather than
    cloudBuild.setVersionVariables in version.json: the version height is the
    number of commits since version.json last changed, so editing that file at
    all would reset the height to 0 and drop every produced version from
    2.0.<height> to 2.0.0.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <NBGV_SetCloudBuildVersionVars>false</NBGV_SetCloudBuildVersionVars>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <PropertyGroup>
    <GitVersionBaseDirectory>$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)</GitVersionBaseDirectory>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
